                        "entry_id": "bc60cb66-7853-34a7-96d5-0be5d9083d95",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An upper-caste landlord in the southern part of Bihar in eastern India."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4162867a-cf32-49c3-a72f-a2c5ab1aa71b",
                                "sense_id": "5744719b-9f33-3ef6-9459-2667b193ab17",
                                "text": "[…] the essay interprets the oral traditions of the outcaste Bhuinyas who have traditionally worked as the kamias or dependent labourers of maliks or upper-caste landlords in the southern part of Bihar in eastern India. […] But the kamias' ties with the maliks predated the designation of the relationship as bondage in the nineteenth century."
                            }
